-- ==========================================
-- MOVEMENT SCRIPT v13
-- ==========================================
-- NEW in v13: CROSSING LASER DETECTION
--
--   When two lasers are both approaching and their paths cross near the
--   player, the script finds the world-space intersection point of the
--   two laser centre-lines and aims the jump over THAT point instead of
--   just past one laser. This clears both beams in a single jump.
--
--   How it works:
--   1. Collect all "threat" lasers (not passed, localZ < AGGRO_DISTANCE).
--   2. For every pair, call findLaserIntersection() which does a 2D
--      closest-approach on the two infinite lines defined by each
--      laser's position + forward vector.
--   3. If the intersection is within MAX_CROSS_DIST of the player AND
--      both lasers are within CROSS_BOTH_DIST, mark it as a crossing event.
--   4. The jump target is set to (intersection XZ) + offset away from the
--      player so the bot lands past BOTH beams.
--   5. Arc prediction is run against BOTH lasers and both must pass before
--      the jump fires.
--
-- All v12 fixes (position-delta move dir, backup on unsafe arc) kept.
-- ==========================================
print("[Movement] v13 loaded")

